.uk/about/researchers/researcher-committee"],["Life as a Researcher at Oxford","https://eng.ox.ac.uk/about/researchers"],["Researcher profiles","https://eng.ox.ac.uk/about/researchers/researcher-profiles"],["Research news","https://eng.ox.ac.uk/news/?topic=research-news"],["Apply now","https://eng.ox.ac.uk/jobs"]],"fullText":"ENGINEERING SCIENCE\nResearch\nEnter the name of an institution or research group\nBiomedical\nChemical and Process\nCivil and Offshore\nControl\nElectrical and Opto-electronic\nEnergy\nEngineering, Entrepreneurship and Management\nInformation\nOur Institutes\nSolid Mechanics and Materials\nThermo-Fluids and Turbomachinery\n\n“The major theme underlying our research portfolio is the application of cross-disciplinary state of the art science to new technologies and applications, using a mixture of theory and experiment”\n\nThe Department of Engineering Science has an international reputation for its research in all the major branches of engineering, and in emerging areas such as biomedical engineering, energy and the environment. We place a strong emphasis on interdisciplinary and collaborative work, both within engineering science and across the physical, medical and life sciences.\n\nThe Department also has an excellent record of engagement with industry, and has generated numerous successful spin-out companies.\n\nResearch is a core component of the Department and we highly value the input and well-being of our research community - find out about life as a Researcher at Oxford, and about our Researcher Committee, which provides representation across all areas of our post-doctoral research body. You can also read profiles of some of our researchers.\n\nResearcher Committee\n\nLife as a Researcher at Oxford\n\nResearcher profiles\n\nResearch news\n\nResearcher vacancies\nAPPLY NOW"}